CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ destroyed across a virtual call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ destroyed across a function-pointer call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ loop: one normal-exit \+ one unwinding destruction: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[except.ctor]/1-3 across indirect calls: function-pointer and virtual-function
removal carry the call-site unwind-cleanup association onto the concrete calls
of their dispatch chains, so destructors run before any handler regardless of
the invocation mechanism; also covers loop-scoped objects.  Runtime-verified
against g++ and clang++.
